**`app/api/finance/refresh-prices/route.ts:30-54`** — Classic N+1: for each investment, two sequential I/O operations happen: a Yahoo Finance HTTP call, then a DB update. With N investments, that's 2N sequential round-trips.

```ts
// CURRENT — N sequential Yahoo calls + N sequential DB writes
for (const inv of investments) {
  const quote = await yahooFinance.quote(yahooTicker);
  await prisma.investment.update({ where: { id: inv.id }, data: { currentPrice } });
}

// FIX — parallel fetches, then batch write
const quotes = await Promise.all(
  investments.map(inv => yahooFinance.quote(TICKER_MAP[inv.ticker] ?? inv.ticker).catch(() => null))
);
const updates = investments
  .map((inv, i) => ({ inv, price: quotes[i]?.regularMarketPrice ?? quotes[i]?.bid ?? null }))
  .filter(({ price }) => price && price > 0);

await Promise.all(
  updates.map(({ inv, price }) =>
    prisma.investment.update({ where: { id: inv.id }, data: { currentPrice: price!, lastUpdated: new Date() } })
  )
);
```

**`app/api/dashboard/home/route.ts:47-49`** — Two separate queries for what could be one:

```ts
// CURRENT — 2 queries
prisma.bodyMetric.findFirst({ orderBy: { date: "desc" } }),           // latest
prisma.bodyMetric.findMany({ orderBy: { date: "desc" }, take: 2, skip: 1 }), // prev

// FIX — 1 query, destructure result
const [latest, prev] = await prisma.bodyMetric.findMany({ orderBy: { date: "desc" }, take: 2 });
// latest = result[0], prev = result[1]
```

---

**`components/DataStreamNumber.tsx:51-65`** — The `useDataStream` hook runs a `requestAnimationFrame` loop that calls `setDigits` every ~55ms, triggering a re-render. The dashboard mounts 5+ `DataStreamNumber` instances simultaneously (hero stats × 3, metric cards × 2), all RAF-animating in parallel for ~1 second on page load. Each `setDigits` call re-renders the parent subtree.

Mitigation: contain the animation to a `span` with a CSS `@keyframes` custom property trick, or at minimum ensure `DataStreamNumber` is not nested inside large animated parents.

**`app/_components/DashboardHome.tsx:283`** — `weightChartData` is recomputed from scratch on every render:

```ts
// CURRENT — runs every render
const weightChartData = (data?.weightHistory ?? []).map(d => ({
  date: format(parseISO(d.date), "d MMM", { locale: fr }),
  Poids: d.value,
  Tendance: d.ma,
}));

// FIX — memoize since data only changes on fetch
const weightChartData = useMemo(() =>
  (data?.weightHistory ?? []).map(d => ({
    date: format(parseISO(d.date), "d MMM", { locale: fr }),
    Poids: d.value,
    Tendance: d.ma,
  })),
[data?.weightHistory]);
```

**`app/taches/_components/TachesClient.tsx:109-111`** — `dayTasks`, `weekTasks`, `allDayDone` recomputed on every render from `initialTasks` prop, which never changes (server component data):

```ts
// FIX
const dayTasks = useMemo(() => initialTasks.filter(t => t.scope === "DAY"), [initialTasks]);
const weekTasks = useMemo(() => initialTasks.filter(t => t.scope === "WEEK"), [initialTasks]);
const allDayDone = useMemo(() => dayTasks.length > 0 && dayTasks.every(t => t.completed), [dayTasks]);
```

---

Every API route is `force-dynamic`, which disables all Next.js caching — appropriate for user-specific mutation routes but unnecessary for read routes:

**`app/api/dashboard/home/route.ts:4`** and **`app/api/finance/route.ts:5`** — Data changes at most a few times per day. Consider revalidation:

```ts
// Replace: export const dynamic = "force-dynamic";
export const revalidate = 60; // ISR: revalidate once per minute
// Or for Next.js 14+ fine-grained:
export const fetchCache = "default-cache";
```

For the finance route, the `days` query param makes ISR impractical, but you can add HTTP cache headers:

```ts
return NextResponse.json(data, {
  headers: { "Cache-Control": "private, max-age=60, stale-while-revalidate=300" },
});
```

**`fmtEuro` — recreated every call** — Both `FinanceClient.tsx:51` and `DashboardHome.tsx:59` create a new `Intl.NumberFormat` object on every invocation:

```ts
// CURRENT — new formatter on every call
function fmtEuro(n: number) {
  return new Intl.NumberFormat("fr-FR", { style: "currency", currency: "EUR", maximumFractionDigits: 0 }).format(n);
}

// FIX — create once at module level
const euroFmt = new Intl.NumberFormat("fr-FR", { style: "currency", currency: "EUR", maximumFractionDigits: 0 });
function fmtEuro(n: number) { return euroFmt.format(n); }
```

---

**`components/DataStreamNumber.tsx:69-83`** — `setTimeout`s inside `useEffect` are **not cleaned up**. If the component unmounts during the animation, the callbacks still fire and call `setDigits` on an unmounted component:

```ts
// CURRENT — leaked timeouts
numericIndices.forEach((idx, order) => {
  setTimeout(() => {      // ← not cleaned up
    setDigits(...);
    setTimeout(() => {    // ← nested, also not cleaned up
      setDigits(...);
    }, 80);
  }, delay + ...);
});

// FIX — track and cancel
const timeoutIds: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout>[] = [];

numericIndices.forEach((idx, order) => {
  const t1 = setTimeout(() => {
    setDigits((prev) => { ... });
    const t2 = setTimeout(() => {
      setDigits((prev) => { ... });
    }, 80);
    timeoutIds.push(t2);
  }, delay + scrambleDuration + slowdownDuration + order * lockInterval);
  timeoutIds.push(t1);
});

return () => {
  if (rafRef.current) cancelAnimationFrame(rafRef.current);
  timeoutIds.forEach(clearTimeout); // ← add this
};
```

---

**`app/api/dashboard/home/route.ts:115-119`** — Moving average uses `slice` + `reduce` per element, O(n×7) total. A sliding window makes it O(n):

```ts
// CURRENT — O(n*k)
const weightWithMA = weightHistory.map((d, i) => {
  const slice = weightHistory.slice(Math.max(0, i - 6), i + 1);
  const ma = slice.reduce((s, x) => s + x.value, 0) / slice.length;
  return { ...d, ma: parseFloat(ma.toFixed(2)) };
});

// FIX — O(n) sliding window
let windowSum = 0;
const windowVals: number[] = [];
const weightWithMA = weightHistory.map((d) => {
  windowVals.push(d.value);
  windowSum += d.value;
  if (windowVals.length > 7) windowSum -= windowVals.shift()!;
  const ma = parseFloat((windowSum / windowVals.length).toFixed(2));
  return { ...d, ma };
});
```

